<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot rates KNP BT Strong Outperformer.</title>
<headline>Lanschot rates KNP BT Strong Outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (01/08)</p>
<p>Company-----Sector-----------------Price---Broker----</p>
<p>KNP BT	paper,office products  47.60   Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: Strong Outperformance</p>
<p>First-half net sales rose 12 pct, net income for ordinary shareholders  up 43 pct to 119 million guilders. Earnings at paper production division  KNP Leykam will benefit from reorganisation and probably from recovering  paper prices. We expect KNP BT to joint with another low cost European  coated paper producer, gaining synergy benefits. Finnish paper group  Enso is most likely because of its position in pulp.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS*    P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     1.92    19.7   5.1    0.85</p>
<p>    1997		  3.50    13.6   5.1    1.50</p>
<p>    1997		  5.00     9.5   4.6    1.75</p>
<p>*NOTE  - earnings per share before extraordinary items.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
